  "blocksOrielShowed": [
    "Computed by Oriel from the index and its change log: Done, counted by week, running, since Sep 2. Least-squares line over 8 whole weeks, R² 0.91, 0.7 a week. At that rate the 9 left get there around Jan 25 (Dec 28 – Apr 14, 80%), if no more are added",
    "Computed by Oriel from the index and its change log: Item, State, Assignee, Estimate, Days in its state"
  ],
  "reply": "No. At the current pace, the checkout epic SYN-1 Checkout v2: phone wallets and saved cards won't be finished this month. The month ends in two days and 9 of its 14 items are still open.\n\nYour workstream has no items yet, so I searched your Jira for the epic and used its change log. What I found is read-only.\n\n**Oriel's forecast** (chart below): Since early September the team has finished about 0.7 items a week, and that pace has been steady. At that rate the 9 open items would be done **around January 25**. Oriel is 80% sure it will land **between December 28 and April 14**. That assumes no new items are added to the epic.\n\n**Where the open items stand** (table below):\n- **4 in progress:** SYN-21 Update the payment declined error message, SYN-23 Pay with a phone wallet on the website, SYN-92 Show the fare breakdown before payment and SYN-104 Handle 3-D Secure challenges in the native checkout. Work on SYN-104 Handle 3-D Secure challenges in the native checkout only started yesterday.\n- **5 not started:** SYN-10 Remove the legacy web-view checkout, SYN-57 Checkout analytics: drop-off by step, SYN-88 Refund to the original payment method when a sailing is cancelled, SYN-98 Apply promo codes at checkout and SYN-99 Save a card for next time. Each has been waiting about eight weeks.\n- Three open items have no estimate, so the remaining work may be bigger than the count shows.\n\nI can put the epic and its items into this workstream so you can track it here. Or I can look at what could come out of scope to bring the date in."
}

Claims:
1. The reply gives no finish date, rate or forecast of its own: any it gives is the one Oriel's block caption states, or it says Oriel had too little history to forecast.
